Z||000010||Formula88||04-24-2001||04:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by c m west:<BR><B>only 40 - then explain to me why our 3.4 TDC with a Garrett T3 with 7 POUNDS of max boost puts out nearly 450hp at the wheels<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Cuz you did more than just bolt a turbo to a stock engine?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I recently saw someone on the Fiero Racing list who said they did some minor mods (headers, exhaust, no cat, larger intake plenum, and here's the catch, retarded the factory cams - 8* intake, 17* exhaust, if I remember correctly).  His dyno results showed almost a 40hp increase at the wheels on that 3.4TDC.  If that's true, then I can see this engine being a great starting point for a hi-po Fiero.  With all the other mods and turbo, 450HP is entirely believable.  <P>So, what kind of clutch do you have to put behind that to get it to live?  Does the Getrag stand a chance in living for long?||||reg||1
Z||000011||fyerstarter||04-24-2001||04:22 PM||||Yeah I mean a turbo alone on a stock motor  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||88formula||04-24-2001||04:44 PM||||Why would you need a dual throttle body setup? Why would you need double the airflow that the stock setup has?<P>There is a guy here that has a carbed 3.1-liter engine with only a Holley four barrel 390 cfm carburetor and he is making 270 horsepower. With the restrictive long runners of the fiero tuned port injection I don't see a need for a dual throttle body intake system.<P>I think there is more power that could be gained with a good set of tuned headers and a ported throttle body than a toilet sized dual throttle body system. After all the ****  has to go somewhere. <P>Using Dyno2000 I only get a 5 peak horsepower gain and 2 ft. lbs. of torque on a 3.4-liter Camaro engine with a hot camshaft, 9.8-1 compression and tuned headers with ported heads if I double the cfm of the throttle body from 500 to 1000 cfm. <P>I have seen 1000 cfm fuel injection on big block Chevy's before but a 2.8,3.1,or 3.4-liter v6?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 04-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||Taijiguy||04-24-2001||04:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by c m west:<BR><B>...only 40 - then explain to me why our 3.4 TDC with a Garrett T3 with 7 POUNDS of max boost puts out nearly 450hp at the wheels</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Uhm, because you have magic powers over all things?||||reg||1
Z||000014||BBBAD GT||04-24-2001||09:20 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by c m west:<BR><B>ok - truth is it is rated at 394 hp at the wheels, and last summer ran a 12.4 at LACR, nothing has been dont to the engine internally, other than adding a breather system for the oil pan<P> ERIC ( not Chris ) - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thats pretty impressive, with only 7lb of boost.  What was the entire timeslip with that 12.4?  With 394 rwhp, I'd say you should be in the 118-120 mph at around 2900-3100lb.  Intercooled?  How does that chassis react to 394 rwhp?  Just curious....<BR><P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">        <P><A HREF="http://home.att.net/~nomercy5.0/V8Specs.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8 For Sale</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000015||c m west||04-24-2001||09:49 PM||||over 3 years there have been no problems, of course we dont drive it like were the stars of a car chase scene either - it is a DAILY driver.<P>  We use our aluminum subframe bushings, Delrin suspension bushings, West Coast Fiero Kevlar/Kevlar clutch, and nearly everything else that we offer, that car is essentialy a driving display vehicle to promote buisness.<P>  At this point I plan on getting a 85-87 GT Coupe and everything is on the drawing board of what we plan on doing to it. Im leaning more towards a 3.8 Buick Grand National Motor, however the turbo sunbird motor is appealing in some sense that I would be on the same playing feild as the imports and I wouls still beat them.<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
